WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.610
(jolly piano music)

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.620
- [Narrator] For Lego
enthusiast, Lucas Lettrick.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.240
These aren't just toys

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.440
- [Lucas] This is the Lego
Creator Palace Cinema.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.270
- [Narrator] They're serious
money-makers that he buys

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:13.680
and sells for profit.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.150
The biggest online database

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:16.830
of collectible Lego sets

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:21.030
lists 1.2 billion worth of
the toys around the world.

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:22.710
- Lego Tron up here

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:24.930
we're in the 3 to $400 range.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:28.440
This Lego Tie Fighter $200 a piece

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.910
is what these are selling.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:32.310
The returns that I typically will see

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:37.310
is somewhere between 150
to 250% on a Lego set.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:38.273
- [Narrator] Researchers say

00:00:38.273 --> 00:00:40.080
Lettrick is one of tens of thousands

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:43.170
who concerned by the recent
volatility of stocks and bonds

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:44.940
are betting on the reliable returns

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:46.920
from this tiny but growing market.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.500
- The average return on other collectibles

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.500
like wines or art, or automobiles, stamps,

00:00:54.642 --> 00:00:57.390
are generally lower than Lego.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.710
- [Narrator] This is niche markets,

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:01.530
a series that examines
small lesser known markets

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:04.330
that despite their size punched
well above their weight.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.200
- There we go.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.790
All right.
- And this one.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:11.310
- [Narrator] Lettrick is an
insurance broker in Pennsylvania

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:12.930
and grew up playing with Lego.

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:15.880
- I kind of got outta Lego,
obviously, like most people do,

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:20.130
but then when I had my first boy Bruce,

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:22.140
we started building some Lego sets

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.240
and that's kinda what
rekindled the passion

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.304
and kinda the memories.

00:01:25.304 --> 00:01:27.090
(playful music)

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:28.860
- [Narrator] This nostalgic
hobby with his children

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.080
turned into a lucrative
investment strategy

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:34.530
when Lettrick walked into a
Target about five years ago.

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:38.640
- I saw a Lego set, Lego
Ninjago, Destiny's Bounty

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.220
and I remember thinking
to myself at that time

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:43.290
I could literally just take this,

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:47.190
put it up online, sell
it, and double my money.

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:48.180
- [Narrator] Since then, he says

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:50.880
he's invested around $65,000

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.510
into building a collection of
Lego's most profitable sets.

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:56.160
The toys in this room typically cost

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:00.300
anywhere from $30 to over $500 at stores.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.450
- So this is the 1989 batmobile.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:04.440
This-
- For Lettrick,

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:06.420
the most important
factor in Lego investing

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:08.730
is knowing how to spot a winning set.

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:11.700
- You think Lego, you might think child,

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:15.600
but Lego is really geared a
lot of their sets nowadays

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.397
towards the adult collectors.

00:02:17.397 --> 00:02:18.570
(ambient music)

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:19.560
- [Narrator] Larger sets like these

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:22.200
target the growing community
of adult fans of Lego

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.750
who call themselves AFOLs.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:26.040
Rather than toys to play with,

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.200
they're usually looking for display pieces

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.720
and can afford these more expensive sets.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.400
- You've got the informational plaque,

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.590
you've got kind of this stand to display

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.660
some of the iconic figures from the movie.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:39.420
So it's a really beautiful set.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:41.220
- [Narrator] To turn a
profit on these kits.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.890
Lettrick, makes sure he
gets in at a low price

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:46.920
so he scours the market for
sets Lego is about to retire

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:48.480
or stop producing.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.520
The official Lego store
and other retailers

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:51.960
usually sell them at a discount

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:53.160
to clear their stock,

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:55.383
sometimes as much as 40% off.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:59.910
- This actually just
retired this past year

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:02.010
and I ended up picking
it up a couple of them

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:04.350
2 or 3 of them for $200 a piece.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.350
Within just a short
period, 6 to 12 months,

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:10.590
this has already jumped up to 400 to $500

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.785
I believe is what this is selling on eBay.

00:03:12.785 --> 00:03:13.800
(playful music)

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:15.480
- [Narrator] But in order
to make a larger profit

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.490
Lettrick says it takes patience

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:21.090
usually holding sets for 2
to 3 years before selling.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:23.310
- Do you want a pristine
set that's sealed?

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.750
That's what a collector's looking for.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:27.240
You wanna make sure you're
storing it on the right shelving.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.890
You wanna make sure that
you're keeping humidity low.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.440
- [Narrator] Lettrick says
he spends 2 to 5 hours a week

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:35.970
on his Lego investments,

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:37.470
and while it's more time-consuming

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:39.540
than other items in his portfolio,

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:41.040
he says his Lego sets have seen

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.020
the most stable growth this year.

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:44.580
- You don't get a lot of fluctuation

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:47.370
with the prices going way down, way up

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.890
like we're obviously seeing
right now with the stock market,

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:50.790
it's very volatile.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:51.690
(ambient music)

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:52.523
- [Narrator] Economists say

00:03:52.523 --> 00:03:54.750
that's because a Lego
market moves more slowly

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.790
than traditional investments.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:59.730
- When some news come to the market

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:03.270
the stock market reacts very
quickly on the same day.

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:06.960
Lego is much less liquid market.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:09.330
- [Narrator] Victoria Dobrynskaya
is an associate professor

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:12.660
at the Higher School of
Economics University in Moscow.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:14.850
Since 2016, she's been specializing in

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:17.460
the Lego secondary or reselling market,

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:19.800
analyzing three decades of financial data

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.600
about the niche investment.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.670
She says the law of supply and demand

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:26.190
helps Lego in the same
way as other collectibles

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:28.470
like luxury watches or fine wine.

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:33.150
- Once a bottle of wine
is open, open and drunk

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:35.220
so it disappears from the market, right?

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:36.510
The same with Lego.

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:37.920
- [Narrator] But what
gives Lego the advantage

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:41.190
over other collectibles, she
says, is it's affordability.

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:43.290
- Generally, other alternative investments

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:44.670
are more expensive

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:48.150
so the potential returns
are somehow lower.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:51.630
I mean, if a Lego set appreciates by $5,

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:56.630
if initially its price was
$1, then it's a huge return.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:58.560
- [Narrator] The Lego Group didn't respond

00:04:58.560 --> 00:04:59.610
to requests for comment

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:01.530
about the growth of the resellers market

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:04.143
and its impact on the
company's product strategy.

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:08.280
- [Lucas] There are times
when you're gonna get

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.960
box damage like that.

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:11.550
- [Narrator] But high-end
Lego sets can come in

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:12.900
thousands of pieces

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:15.360
some of which may be
rare or newly designed.

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:17.970
So buyers expect the
cardboard boxes that hold them

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:21.060
to remain sealed and in
near-perfect condition.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:23.100
- When you buy them distantly on eBay

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:25.770
or on some other platform,
you cannot check it.

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:30.150
So you need to be sure
that it is fully sealed,

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:32.190
because if a rare part is missing

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:34.246
that would be a very big problem.

00:05:34.246 --> 00:05:35.079
(playful music)

00:05:35.079 --> 00:05:36.630
- [Narrator] This niche
market is also at the mercy

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:38.130
of pop culture trends

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:40.770
where the franchises and
themes investors buy today

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:43.290
may not be relevant years down the road.

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:45.690
- That's just kinda part of
doing business and investment,

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:47.700
sometimes you win, sometimes
you lose a little bit,

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.710
but typically if you do it right

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:51.160
it all shakes out in the end.

